        "date_dead_since": null,
        "date_published": "2026-05-17T05:30:14+00:00",
        "description": "<p>Nowadays I review a lot of code locally that was written by llms. I used to review my own code using git + delta. It started to feel limiting with the amount of code written by llms.<p>When looking at a large diff on Friday I pointed an llm at diffs.com and trees.software and told it to build an app. It only took 16 minutes, is extremely fast for large diffs, beautiful and minimal.<p>Today I polished it up and added all the features that I need. It has file filters, search, an llm walkthrough mode, and review comments that you can paste back into your llm.<p>I will be using Codiff a lot, and can finally review the large diff from Friday that led me to build this  If you like it, fork it!</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Comments URL: <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48166275\">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48166275</a></p>\n<p>Points: 6</p>\n<p># Comments: 3</p>",
